{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/595420-sidereal-birthday-party-hijinks","id":595420,"title":"Sidereal birthday party hijinks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-18T23:56:21-07:00","id":595420,"title":"Sidereal birthday party hijinks","content":"In the solo game I'm running, a Chosen of Journeys NPC's 14th birthday is soon and will be getting 20-30 Sidereal and spirit friends to attend the party. The party will either be in the Solar's 5-dot manse which is staffed by about 500 1st-circle demons and is constantly creating new rooms, or it will be on an unnaturally tall mountain where an Alchemical scout's outpost has been under siege by a Raksha for about a year.<br /> <br /> I know with so many Sidereals in one place Limit Breaks might happen but what other fun nonsense might occur either in the manse or on the mountain, presumably after the Solar finds out it's occupied and possibly does something about the issue?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6360-yushichan","name":"Yushichan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6360_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T00:33:51-07:00","id":595460,"title":"","content":"1. The drugs and drink - the various drugs of Heaven are the finest and most potent, sure. They've also got the most exotic. Blow which gives you temporary mutations? Hallucinogens which give you synchronized hallucinations? Clouds of smoke which form varicolored wonderlands in the air, complete with tiny cloud-protagonists acting out epic tales? All of that is a big check.<br /> <br /> 2. Pattern Spider Wha? - Sidereals pretty much ignore Resplendent Destinies, but when everyone's drunk and high and having a great time, the guy with Pattern Spider Touch becomes the absolute life of the party. Oh man, nice, where did you get a juggling flying cat? Also, where's Ted?<br /> <br /> 3. Dance Dance Revolution - I assume that at least one of the guests will be a Joybringer. Once they flare that anima, everyone in the room is a master dancer. Even better, have the DJ pop out an Easily Accepted Proposition to force synchronized and spontaneous musicals.<br /> <br /> 4. The Wyldest Prank - The most useless Larceny Charm is Conning Chaos Technique. It's not fatal, it's expensive and the benefits are minimal. But what it can do is be an hilarious prank when causality starts cutting out around the target.<br /> <br /> 5. Where Dreams Come To Life - Speaking of SMA, do any of the guests have Quicksilver Hand of Dreams style? If so, they could potentially be whipping out Raksha-like figments for entertainment purposes. Stupid dream animals? Animated pornographic murals? A thousand dancing teddy bears orbiting near the ceiling? Whatever you'd like!<br /> <br /> 6. My Only Regret Is I have Clownitis - Did you know that the SMA about disease allows you to make your own supernatural diseases? Did you know that instead of having dangerous effects, they can just do stupid things like making your ears glow or force you to talk backwards for a bit? Shit, it doesn't matter. Try the wrong drink, kiss the wrong girl and suddenly you can only moonwalk.<br /> <br /> 7. Oh My Gods - Read some of those spirit charms, man. Manipulating elements or domains are obviously there, that's easy stuff. But think about the visuals- one water spirit and all the fountains are sporting water sculptures. Clear dance floors in mid air? People frozen in time with silly expressions on their faces? Shapeshifting? It's all there.<br /> <br /> 8. Danger - A Yu-Shan party can be as dangerous as the ST wants. You could play it up as a silly episode by filling it with exotic nonsense which vanishes the next day, sure. On the other hand, a more malicious (or interested) Joybringer can magically re-arrange emotions, loves and alignments with a touch. End up with the wrong dance partner and you're at risk of being someone's sex slave forever. Any one of those drugs could actually be a spiritual parasite which tries to replace your mind. Hell, if there's a powerful enough Sidereal there, they could try to replace your soul with friendly handshake. This could be a very, very dangerous social event.<br /> <br /> Good luck!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T01:07:37-07:00","id":595476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercury</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/595420-sidereal-birthday-party-hijinks?p=595460#post595460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">condensed</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, Mercury! You give your Chosen Ride as a favored ability so I'm sure you'd be the type to know a lot about the possible debauchery in a party primarily attended by guests from Yu-Shan. I can imagine drunk Sidereals from opposing factions making nonsensical arguments why their side is better than the other and some spirits leaving the party to wander around Gem and create lots of God-Blooded since that's what spirits do whenever they're allowed near mortals.<br /> <br /> This party could in fact cause or even be the fated doom of Gem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6360-yushichan","name":"Yushichan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6360_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T07:01:11-07:00","id":595590,"title":"","content":"Last time I threw a birthday bash in Yu Shan (well, technically a &quot;congratulations on Exalting&quot; bash for a newly Chosen servant of Mars), me and a few circle mates loaded up on the ingredients for the thaumaturgical ritual that changes the colors of stuff.<br /> <br /> ...we, uh, turned the entire Crimson Panoply of Victory, and the fields around it, Robins Egg Blue. It was hilarious! <br /> <br /> The Maidens remained inscrutable as always, but I'm pretty sure Mars smiled at me at the Carnival. Either she thought it was funny or I am so very screwed...maybe both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T07:06:08-07:00","id":595594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/595420-sidereal-birthday-party-hijinks?p=595590#post595590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last time I threw a birthday bash in Yu Shan (well, technically a &quot;congratulations on Exalting&quot; bash for a newly Chosen servant of Mars), me and a few circle mates loaded up on the ingredients for the thaumaturgical ritual that changes the colors of stuff.<br /> <br /> ...we, uh, turned the entire Crimson Panoply of Victory, and the fields around it, Robins Egg Blue. It was hilarious!<br /> <br /> The Maidens remained inscrutable as always, but I'm pretty sure Mars smiled at me at the Carnival. Either she thought it was funny or I am so very screwed...maybe both.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh dear, well hopefully if the option is screwed it's not that kind of screwed, since if it is that kind of screwed, well, things might be a bit screwed.<br /> Also was that little recoloring ritual temporary or did some poor god of janitors have to scrub the whole thing red again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T07:44:41-07:00","id":595628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/595420-sidereal-birthday-party-hijinks?p=595590#post595590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">condensed</div> </div> </div> </div>I can imagine an ST with an extremely flanderized view of the Maidens would make Mars jump to conclusions and preemptively declare war on Venus.<br /> <br /> Also I should point out the party will be in Creation, not Yu-Shan. In or near Gem to be exact.<br /> <br /> I could also imagine would-be guests using the Loom like one of those bad neighborhood checkers and deciding to avoid the party since Gem is so doomed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6360-yushichan","name":"Yushichan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6360_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T08:25:27-07:00","id":595662,"title":"","content":"You don't need to worry about Gem blowing up unless the local Spirit Courts find out and decide to crash your party. If the Gemlord beneath Gem decides this party is so hot that it needs to show up you're going to have problems.<br /> <br /> Of course you get similar kinds of problems if the locals get offended you didn't invite them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T08:40:28-07:00","id":595664,"title":"","content":"How does a sessile gemlord go to a party, anyway?<br /> Now, it can send proxies to crash the party. But that's not necessarily going to blow up Gem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T08:55:37-07:00","id":595680,"title":"","content":"Someone'll set off some pretty bitchin' fireworks for the birthday girl and then things just go out of control from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T08:57:52-07:00","id":595682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/595420-sidereal-birthday-party-hijinks?p=595664#post595664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does a sessile gemlord go to a party, anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>This exalted, the number of ways is uncountable. An immediate method that come to mind is to convince, or mind control, a sorcerer at the party to summon it and not bind it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T22:50:38-07:00","id":596517,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that many Sidereals aren't going to get time off all at once. I mean, that's a whole mess of Sidereals suddenly not doing their job for one day. And in Creation. In one of the most volatile and dangerous cities in the Direction. In a giant manse that is constantly changing and is staffed by several hundred demons.<br /> <br /> It's going to look weird. Kejak and/or Ura are probably going to &quot;crash&quot; it to investigate and make sure you're not planning a coup or something.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit:Wait..you're trucking with one or more Solars? Ohhh, you're just TRYING to touch off something nasty, aren't you?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":". 07-20-2015, 02:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}